  "caveats": [
    "R5 and R6 are single seed. R6 is the highest xsim-hard number here but has no interval. It is a lead, not a finding.",
    "The significance test compares seed 42 of each arm. The three-seed spread is separate evidence pointing the same way, but it is not the same test.",
    "Per-query vectors exist for R3 and R4 seed 42 only. Any other pair needs a re-run.",
    "Run-to-run drift on an identical command reaches 0.0024 on xsim-hard. R3 seed 42 gave 0.8444 then 0.8461, and R4 seed 42 gave 0.8592 then 0.8616, when both were retrained to capture per-query vectors. R0 reproduced exactly, so the nondeterminism enters with hard-negative mining, not with plain training.",
    "That drift is larger than the bootstrap interval's lower bound of +0.0011. The conclusion still holds on the seed evidence, where the lowest R4 run (0.8574) is above the highest R3 run (0.8461), but the lower end of the interval should not be read as a floor on the effect."
  ]
